# Desygn AI core rules

- Read `AGENTS.md` before making architectural changes.
- Extend canonical packages instead of creating parallel V2/V3 implementations.
- Keep standards, scoring, permissions, identifiers, policy and persisted contracts deterministic and tested.
- AI may explain, recommend and plan from evidence; it must not become the only definition of a product rule.
- Reuse `@desygn/ui` tokens/primitives before creating local UI equivalents.
- Validate external/model data at trust boundaries.
- Never expose secrets in frontend, plugin, fixtures, logs, docs or generated files.
- Never add proprietary/customer content to this public repo: no private client branding, internal screenshots, copied internal checklists, documents, business identifiers, or customer-specific design rules. Use synthetic neutral examples and public standards.
- Do not suppress required build/test failures with `continue-on-error`.
- A reusable component change must update tests, Storybook and machine-readable registry metadata.
- UI changes require accessibility and responsive verification; visual changes require visual verification when the pipeline is available.
- Never publish/version/release unless explicitly requested by the owner.
